s","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ismaelrumzan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ismaelrumzan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ismaelrumzan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ismaelrumzan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ismaelrumzan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-1050710571/sdk/commits/d78c8e5eb60464ea4ac8277475491b36693c1c51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T16:41:17Z","email":"ismael@vercel.com","name":"Ismael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T16:41:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix auto-merge: use workflow_run trigger instead of pull_request (#235)\n\nThe pull_request: [opened] trigger never fires for Speakeasy PRs\nbecause the generation workflow creates them using GITHUB_TOKEN, and\nGitHub silently drops events from GITHUB_TOKEN to prevent loops.\n\nThe workflow_run trigger is exempt from this limitation. Now triggers\nwhen the Test workflow completes successfully on a speakeasy-sdk-regen\nbranch, finds the associated PR, and enables auto-merge.\n\nMade-with: Cursor","tree":{"sha":"4a1406db8e3aa5c7833c64aa1fa5fbb1b10fbaaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-1050710571/sdk/git/trees/4a1406db8e3aa5c7833c64aa1fa5fbb1b10fbaaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-1050710571/sdk/git/commits/d78c8e5eb60464ea4ac8277475491b36693c1c51","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a1406db8e3aa5c7833c64aa1fa5fbb1b10fbaaf\nparent 867003f3c30b46a84e41470e39bedafa040d9768\nauthor Ismael <ismael@vercel.com> 1772815277 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772815277 -0700\n\nFix auto-merge: use workflow_run trigger instead of pull_request (#235)\n\nThe pull_request: [opened] trigger never fires for Speakeasy PRs\nbecause the generation workflow creates them using GITHUB_TOKEN, and\nGitHub silently drops events 